				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Anthem is a guild which strives to be the best we can at raiding. 
<br />
This means that fast communication and quick response times is as important as gear and numbers. 
<br />
Therefore we have developed an example UI that will allow PMs and others to react fast and precise and make sure said persons wont miss crucial raid info. 
<br />

<br />
Please see picture below:
<br />
<img src="http://anthemguild.com/boards/files/clericui.jpg" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
Introduction to UI 
<br />

<br />
First of all. To filter out your different types of text youll recieve in game (that could be rampage. channel 1. Guild. tells) rightclick on main chatwindow to create new chatwindow.. then you rightclick on this new window and choose filter.. here is a long list of different types of messages.. Filter the ones you want into what window.
<br />

<br />
If you have more than one channel in a chat window color the channels in different colors, with the most important ones in the brightest colors. This is done in option and then colors. 
<br />

<br />
The main chat (Purple square): 
<br />
This is here your main concern lies. Here you put the chat that is important for you. That often being group, raid, guild, important channels. But add all here you can’t afford to miss. 
<br />

<br />
Chat 1 (Blue square): 
<br />
This is tell window. If you have a chat dedicated to tells you will hardly ever loose it. And trust me... You don’t want to not see tells you get. This window makes requests for buffs and actions answered fast and smooth. No one should be without. 
<br />
Did you know that /RT makes you target the person who send you a tell last?  Does wonders for fast buffing. 
<br />

<br />
Chat 2 (Red square): 
<br />
Important combat-info here. That be spells casted (complete heal and gate from mobs) or whatever melee combat spam is important. 
<br />
Alternative you can put semi important channels in here, Chances are you will miss some, hence the not too important stuff should go here. 
<br />

<br />
Chat 3 (Green square): 
<br />
This is for spam. Your hits, you being hit, the works. All the crap you cant turn on and is flooding your other chats… get it there. 
<br />

<br />
Effects (yellow square): 
<br />
Know what effects you need and which classes that cast them. Anthem rebuffing and buffing of latecomers is handled in tells. You tell for buffs and get the quick (see chat 1 info). You receive requests for buffs and give them fast. The faster we buff the faster we can kill again.
<br />

<br />
Attached is a zip file with the ini file that you can rename to character1_eci.ini to get the layout in the picture at a screen resolution of 1024 x 768. it has to placed in your main EQ folder.
<br />

<br />
Any comments, queries or feedback please send me a PM
<br />

<br />
Silverfalcon - Camp cleric of Anthem</span>
